{"extract": "Alejandro Oscar Finocchiaro (born 27 August 1967) is an Argentine lawyer and politician who served as Minister of Education, Culture, Science and Technology of Argentina. Previously he was general director of Culture and Education of the province of Buenos Aires and Secretary of Educational Policies and Teaching Career in the Autonomous City of Buenos Aires. Since 2021, he has been a National Deputy elected in Buenos Aires Province.", "links": [{"ns": 10, "title": "Template:Infobox officeholder", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "2021 Argentine legislative election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Argentina", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Argentine Chamber of Deputies", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Autonomous city", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Buenos Aires", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Buenos Aires Province", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Cambiemos", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Esteban Bullrich", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Incumbent", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Mauricio Macri", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Ministry of Education (Argentina)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Nicolás Trotta", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Republican Proposal", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "San Fernando Partido", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "University of Buenos Aires", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "University of San Andrés", "exists": true}]}